# Map rows in db-mapping.js

Query functions return rows through `dbMapping.map.*`. Do not translate columns to JS fields inside `query-*.js`.

1. Use an existing map in `src-electron/db/db-mapping.js` when the row is that entity.
2. Extend that map when the query adds columns for the same entity. Add the new fields only when the column is present (`'COLUMN' in x`) if older queries do not select it.
3. Add a new map only when no existing map describes the row.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — column mapping copied into the query
rows.map((row) => ({
  id: row.DATA_TYPE_ID,
  name: row.NAME
}))

// ❌ BAD — rebuild a fake row to call the map
dbMapping.map.dataType({
  DATA_TYPE_ID: type.id,
  NAME: type.name
})

// ✅ GOOD — map the real row once
rows.map(dbMapping.map.dataType)
```

Grouping or filtering mapped records can stay in the query. The field names themselves come from the map.
